      en: "Luoyang in Henan Province is one of the four great ancient capitals of China, with a history spanning over 3,000 years. The city is home to the Longmen Grottoes, a masterpiece of Buddhist cave art and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Luoyang is also famously known as the city of peonies, which bloom in full each spring.",
